cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  How Finely Must We Slice? Detector Granularity in Cosmic-Ray
  Muon Track Reconstruction
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sutanto
    given-names: Callie Angeline
  - family-names: Karyanto
    given-names: Lorenzo
year: 2026
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Geant4 simulation study of how the number of active sampling
  layers in a muon tracker affects angular resolution, at fixed
  total stack height. Resolution improves to a minimum at N = 64
  and degrades thereafter as multiple Coulomb scattering in the
  added scintillator overtakes the benefit of extra measurement
  points.
